label bait
[signal arg="bg:cafeteria_morning"]
Enriko: They've been asking around about Veldero. Which class he's in, which corridors he walks alone.
Enriko: Subtle as a brick, both of them, but Veldero hasn't noticed yet.
Lan (Talk): Why Veldero and not me?
Enriko: Because you're the one who scared them, and cowards don't go back for seconds against the thing that scared them.
Enriko: They go for the softest target next to it.
Enriko: They'll corner him somewhere quiet, rough him up, and let word get back to you. Bait.
Lan (Default): That's a stupid plan.
Enriko: A stupid plan executed by stupid people, which is worse, because they won't know to stop when it's already gone wrong.
Enriko: Keep an eye on him. I'll keep my ear out.
set {aff_enriko} += 1
Three days later, the ear paid off.
label confrontation
[signal arg="bg:east_cloister"]
The message came from a first-year Lan barely recognized, breathless from running. East cloister, now, they've got your friend.
Han: There he is. Wondered how long it'd take. We're just having a conversation. Your friend was explaining how sorry he is for the mint incident.
Veldero: I wasn't.
Veldero got a shove into the wall for it that made Lan's vision go narrow.
- Joint lock and a warning
	Lan (Combat): (No sword. Amir's rule lives in the hall, but I've got my own rule, and it doesn't involve giving these two a montante story.)
- Keep it quick and quiet
	Lan (Smug): (Two boys. Four seconds. Make it look like luck.)
He closed the distance before Jack finished turning, caught the wrist already cocking back,
and put Jack on the ground with a joint lock from six years of settling arguments with men larger than either of them.
Han lunged anyway. Lan sidestepped and put his momentum into the wall.
The whole thing took four seconds, and looked like Lan had gotten lucky twice in a row.
Lan (Default): That's the last time either of you touches him. Not because I'll tell someone. Because next time I show up, I won't be this restrained about it.
label bandage
Leonora heard about it before dinner, the way she seemed to hear about everything eventually.
Leonora (Default): You're bleeding. Sit down.
Lan (Talk): It's nothing.
Leonora (Default): I didn't ask if it was something. I have a healing kit.
Lan (Smug): You carry a healing kit.
Leonora (Smile): I carry several things people don't expect a princess to carry. It's proven useful more than once.
Leonora (Default): You keep putting yourself in the way of things that aren't yours to carry,
Leonora (Default): for reasons you won't explain, at a cost you don't weigh the way anyone sensible would.
Leonora (Default): It's a puzzle, and I don't like unsolved puzzles standing this close to me.
Lan (Smug): So this is a professional interest.
Leonora (Default): Call it what you like. I intend to keep watching you closely until I understand why.
Leonora (Default): Consider that a warning, not a courtesy. And don't bleed on my bandages again. They're not free.
set {aff_leonora} += 1
label eastwing
[signal arg="bg:east_wing_night"]
The abandoned east wing had been Lan's since his second week.
Three empty classrooms, a hallway with a hole in the roof that let moonlight through in a long silver stripe,
and no one who ever looked for a student there after curfew.
Liesel (Default): That footwork. You keep dropping your back foot at an angle. Is that deliberate?
Lan (Talk): It's called Nachreisen. Following after.
Lan (Talk): You let the opponent's momentum carry them past you, and the angle sets you up to close the gap the instant they're off balance.
Liesel (Smile): You explain this like a teacher.
Lan (Smile): I had good ones. Long ago.
Dialog/Ilia (Goof): Okay. I was expecting a ghost, or a very large rat, and instead I find this. This is so much more interesting.
Lan (Acting): This isn't what it looks like.
Dialog/Ilia (Goof): It looks like a rank {rank} doing footwork I've seen maybe three people at this academy manage cleanly,
Dialog/Ilia (Goof): with a sword I've never seen, in a hallway that officially doesn't exist on the building map.
Lan (Sus): (Iliako Fengari. Ninth overall in the whole academy.)
Lan (Sus): (First in her year, and second-years are measured only against second-years.)
Lan (Sus): (Two separate systems, and both of them say this is not a fair fight.)
Lan (Talk): Ilia. I need you not to mention this to anyone.
Dialog/Ilia (Happy): Obviously. I'm not going to tell the faculty you've been sandbagging. Where's the fun in that?
Dialog/Ilia (Happy): But I want something for my silence. I refuse to be boring.
Lan (Default): What do you want?
Dialog/Ilia (Happy): A sparring partner. A real one. Full effort.
Dialog/Ilia (Happy): I train alone because there's no one at my level willing to go all out with me.
Dialog/Ilia (Happy): Everyone's too worried about hurting the princess of Nordvinter's favorite export, or getting hurt themselves.
Dialog/Ilia (Happy): Twice a week, here, and I keep your secret as long as you keep showing up.
Dialog/Ilia (Def): One condition. Blade only. No gi, no shir. If I brought everything I've got it wouldn't be sparring, it'd be a funeral.
- Deal
	set {aff_ilia} += 1
	Lan (Smile): Deal.
- Deal, and you owe me tea
	set {aff_ilia} += 2
	Lan (Smug): Deal. And every session ends with tea, on you.
	Dialog/Ilia (Happy): Oh, I like you. Deal.
set {ilia_deal} = 1
Dialog/Ilia (Happy): Wonderful! Now that that's settled, since I'm already here and you're already holding that ridiculous sword, how about we start tonight?
[signal arg="chapter_end:ch07"]
[end_timeline]
